next best step in management?','{"A":"Induction of labor.","B":"Cesarean delivery.","C":"Steroids.","D":"Pelvic ultrasound.","E":"Admission to the hospital and arrange for blood transfusion."}','D','When a breech presentation suspected by manual exam, ultrasonography is needed as the next best step in management for confirmation, as well as evaluation of maternal pelvis, the fetal size and viability. This should be considered in every future
visit. Breech presentation has the chance to spontaneously turn into cephalic 36 to 37 weeks. Once the breech position persists beyond this time, the chance of spontaneous version reduces to 25%. It is recommended that all women with breech
presentation be offered an external cephalic version provided that there is no contraindication and cesarean delivery is not indicated for other reasons..','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"434","duplicate_group_id":"exact-855763af7c94","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"6daad8676fb67f1974cf","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1127,"source_qid":"434"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"6daad8676fb67f1974cf","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_year":2023,"source_page":1127,"source_qid":"434","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"A 23-year old Asian woman comes to your clinic at 36 weeks gestation. She was diagnosed with breech at 32 weeks. She is not in labor and manual examination of the uterus is suggestive of breech position. Which one of the following would be the\nnext best step in management?","options":{"A":"Induction of labor.","B":"Cesarean delivery.","C":"Steroids.","D":"Pelvic ultrasound.","E":"Admission to the hospital and arrange for blood transfusion."},"source_answer":"D","source_explanation":"When a breech presentation suspected by manual exam, ultrasonography is needed as the next best step in management for confirmation, as well as evaluation of maternal pelvis, the fetal size and viability. This should be considered in every future\nvisit. Breech presentation has the chance to spontaneously turn into cephalic 36 to 37 weeks. Once the breech position persists beyond this time, the chance of spontaneous version reduces to 25%. It is recommended that all women with breech\npresentatio