port strap below the elbow acts as a counterforce brace for Janet and is the best choice among the given options.\n(Option A) Immobilization of the elbow has been shown to be inferior to counterforce bracing below the elbow in pain reduction and increasing grip strength.\n(Option B) Intralesional corticosteroid injection is reserved for patients with refractory severe pain and disability despite conservative management. Corticosteroid injection is\nassociated with a rapid response in short term but poorer outcome in long term.\n(Options D and E) Lateral epicondylitis is a tendinosis rather than tendinitis with minimum or absent inflammatory changes on histopathology. Despite the absence of apparent\ninflammation, NSAIDs either topical or oral (if not contraindicated) have shown benefit in short term (up to 14 days) in some studies. Although controversial, they are often used for\npatients with lateral epicondylitis, specially during the acute initial phase. Diclofenac is the preferred NSAIDs as it has showed efficacy in some studies (to date naproxen has proved\nnot more effective than placebo).","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","drug","management","treatment"],"likely_visual_question":true,"parser_confidence":"very_high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"176555da99ec005eb342a62a916608988f5f435c","duplicate_group_id":"exact-176555da99ec","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"0a13f21fa3edbc2aee63","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1176,"source_qid":"1237"}]}',1,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.d