umstantiality’ best. Circumstantiality occurs when the patient drifts from one\ntopic to the other but eventually returns to the starting point. In other words, if a question is\nimagined as a destination, there are many detours, but the destination is reached at the end. Unlike\ncircumstantiality, patients with derailment (option D) (loosening of association) never come back\nto the topic they started off with. Tangentiality (option E) or tangential speech is a milder form of\nderailment in which there is a hint linking two consecutive topics (whales and the whale oil that\nlight up the world [whale oil in the past had industrial use including for lighting and as fuel]).\nFlight of ideas (option A) is characterized by over-productive speech with rapid shifting from one\ntopic to another. There is often a hint in the previous topic leading to the next one. In the flight of\nideas, there is a subjective feeling that the thoughts are racing. In the flight of ideas, the topic\nspoken by the patient is organized but over-productive and in excess of details. In other words, the\ngeneral concept of the current topic is adequately understood, but a hint in one part leads the\npatient to another. This patient follows a direct line made of pieces that are relevant and justify his\nsanity and that of his family for that matter, rather than jumping from one topic to another. \nIn word salad (option B), the patient throws words together without any sensible and intelligible\nmeaning.","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"low","currentness_keywords":[],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"94d8f0302a6b97fa0b4bdd259d54743951168743","duplicate_group_id":"exact-94d8f0302a6b","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"226fdb1a701ac559b08b","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1470,"source_qid":null}]}',1,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=excluded.visual_url,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk,record_json=excluded.record_json,active_quiz=excluded.active_quiz,import_version=excluded.import_version,imported_at=excluded.imported_at;
