an attempted suicide. He is started on sertraline. For how long he should receive the medication?','{"A":"Six months.","B":"One year.","C":"Two years.","D":"Five years.","E":"Life-long."}','D','For most patients with depression the medical treatment should be continued for at least 6 months
to ideally 12 months.
In the following situations, however, the duration of therapy should be extended to 3 to 5 years:
Two episodes of major depression in 5 years
Three previous episodes of major depression
Depression with psychotic features
Depression with a serious suicidal attempt
 After 3-5 years, the patient should be reassessed for the need for further management. Some
patient might need lifelong antidepressant therapy.
As this patient has had a suicidal attempt, he should receive antidepressant therapy for at least 3-5
years.','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"508","duplicate_group_id":"exact-b6143781f70a","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"a2c63350a14424e5301f","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1476,"source_qid":"508"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"a2c63350a14424e5301f","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_year":2023,"source_page":1476,"source_qid":"508","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"A 27-year-old man is found to have major depression after he has psychiatric evaluation following\nan attempted suicide. He is started on sertraline. For how long he should receive the medication?","options":{"A":"Six months.","B":"One year.","C":"Two years.","D":"Five years.","E":"Life-long."},"source_answer":"D","source_explanation":"For most patients with depression the medical treatment should be continued for at least 6 months\nto ideally 12 months.\nIn the following situations, however, the duration of therapy should be extended to 3 to 5 years:\nTwo episodes of major depression in 5 years\nThree previous episodes of major depression\nDepression with psychotic features\nDepression with a serious suicidal attempt\n After 3-5 years, the patient should be reassessed for the need for further management. Some\npatient might need lifelong antidepressant therapy.\nAs this patient has had a suicidal attempt, he should receive antidepressant therapy for at least 3-5\nyears.","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","curr